				<description>&lt;p&gt;To make your extra mouse buttons work on Linux Mint (I&amp;rsquo;ve tested it with v15) follow all the steps listed in this &lt;a href=&#34;http://lotphelp.com/lotp/lotp-guide-logitech-mx-mouse-ubuntu&#34; title=&#34;Using Your Logitech MX Mouse with Ubuntu&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;tutorial&lt;/a&gt; &lt;svg xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 12 16&#34; width=&#34;12&#34; height=&#34;16&#34;&gt;&lt;path fill-rule=&#34;evenodd&#34; d=&#34;M11 10h1v3c0 .55-.45 1-1 1H1c-.55 0-1-.45-1-1V3c0-.55.45-1 1-1h3v1H1v10h10v-3zM6 2l2.25 2.25L5 7.5 6.5 9l3.25-3.25L12 8V2H6z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA; except the step 4 :)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Once you get to step 4, use this key mappings to make the &amp;lsquo;zoom&amp;rsquo; and &amp;lsquo;switch between windows&amp;rsquo; buttons work as on windows.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
